      "id": "t1",
      "instruction": "Required solver: OpenSees.\nUse OpenSees to analyze a two-story steel frame with 3.6 m story heights and two unequal spans of 5.4 m and 6.0 m. All three column bases are fixed. The geometry/member tables in the public input replace the source drawing. D applies global downward 10 kN/m and L applies global downward 8 kN/m to every beam on both floors as separate load cases. Define C1 = 1.2D + 1.4L. Report ux, uz and ry at every beam-column joint on each floor, Fx, Fz and My at all column bases, and M2 at both ends of all four floor beams, separately for D, L and C1. Retain the original case loads and the explicit combination factors.\n\nUse all public appendices. Report the complete requested numerical table and the required summaries.",
      "state": 1,
      "expectation": "analyze",
